{title: O Master Let Me Walk with Thee}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]O Master, [F]let me [Dm]walk with [G]Thee
[G7]In lowly [C]paths of [D]service [G]free
[G7]Tell me Thy [C]secret, [F]help me [G]bear
The [F]strain of [Dm]toil, the [G]fret of [C]care.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Help me the [F]slow of [Dm]heart to [G]move
[G7]By some clear, [C]winning [D]word of [G]love
[G7]Teach me the [C]wayward [F]feet to [G]stay
And [F]guide them [Dm]in the [G]homeward [C]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]Teach me Thy [F]patience; [Dm]still with [G]Thee
[G7]In closer, [C]dearer [D]compan[G]y
[G7]In work that [C]keeps faith [F]sweet and [G]strong
In [F]trust that [Dm]triumphs [G]over [C]wrong.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C]In hope that [F]sends a [Dm]shining [G]ray
[G7]Far down the [C]future's [D]broad'ning [G]way
[G7]In peace that [C]only [F]Thou canst [G]give
With [F]Thee, O [Dm]Master, [G]let me [C]live.
{end_of_verse}
